      "id": 118403,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-09-19T15:08:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I left H as 2 and technically the game is setup to do just two players but most villains seem balanced better around 3-4</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I might have misunderstood you, but the game is balanced for 3-5 heroes; it can be played with 2 players if one or both are playing a second hero. Obviously, we're talking homerules, here, but…  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>In any case, GTG has stated H is only balanced at 3, 4, or 5.</p>",
